>> title: Tonkotsu Ramen
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: pork, japanese, ramen, noodles, assembly
>> counters: Ramen Shop
>> aka: tonkotsu ramen, tonkotsu, 豚骨ラーメン, とんこつラーメン, Hakata ramen, pork bone ramen, white ramen, a bowl of tonkotsu
>> pairs-with: tonkotsu-broth, shio-tare, mayu, ramen-noodles, chashu
>> servings: 1
>> time: 10 min

>> step: Assembly, not cooking. Everything is already hot, the bowl goes together in ninety seconds, and it is eaten immediately.
Assembly, not cooking.

>> step: spoon the tare and mayu into a scalded bowl
Ladle @shio tare{1 1/2%Tbs}(22 mL) and @mayu{1%tsp}(5 mL) into a scalded #ramen bowl{}.

>> step: boiling broth in, stir once
Pour @tonkotsu broth{1 1/2%cups}(350 mL; at a full boil) into @&(~1)tare and oil{} and stir once, no more.

>> step: boil 15 sec, drain hard
Boil @ramen noodles{5%oz}(140 g; 1.5 mm straight) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L; hard-boiling, unsalted) ~boil{15%sec}, then lift them out and shake the basket hard three or four times.

>> step: lay the noodles in, straightened with chopsticks
Lift @&(~1)drained noodles{} into @&(~2)seasoned broth{} and straighten them into one direction with chopsticks so they lie flat rather than knotting.

>> step: lay the toppings, serve at once
Lay @chāshū{3%slices}(warmed), @kikurage{2%Tbs}(soaked and shredded), @beni shoga{1%Tbs}(red pickled ginger), @scallion{1%stalk}(thinly sliced) and @toasted sesame seeds{1%tsp} over @&(~1)bowl{} and take it to the table.
